title: $:/plugins/tiddlywiki/hive/readme

! Hive storage plugin

Saves a wiki to [[https://hive.blog|Hive]] as a single post with one reply per tiddler, and loads it back again.

!! Requirements

* The [[https://github.com/hivewallet/hive-keychain|Hive Keychain]] browser extension, which signs the transactions. The plugin never has access to your keys.
* A Hive account with enough Hive Power to publish posts.

!! How it works

The wiki is published as:

* one ''root post'' in the configured category — this is the wiki's Hive presence (the entry point). The standalone app (loaded via the hive-shim) should read this root post and load all tiddlers from its replies. The root post body is a readable index; the canonical wiki metadata is in `json_metadata.tw5`.
* one ''reply'' per published tiddler, nested underneath the root post (or underneath the reply of its parent tiddler when the nesting is set to ''path''). The HTML app shell does not need to be rewritten to update tiddlers — only replies are added/updated/marked removed. The root post may reference the app URL via the ''App URL'' setting.

!! Publishing

Publishing is always explicit. Nothing is sent to the blockchain until the ''Save to Hive'' button in the control panel is pressed. The plugin first reads the current replies of the root post, compares them with the local tiddlers, and then broadcasts only the operations that are needed.

!! Loading

Loading reads the root post and all of its replies, and then adds the tiddlers to the wiki. The permlink of the root post is remembered by the plugin, so the wiki can be loaded again with a single click. It can also be given explicitly in the control panel, or with the `permlink` attribute of the action widget.

!! Action widgets

* `<$button><$action-hivesave/>Save to Hive</$button>` saves the wiki to Hive.
* `<$button><$action-hiveload permlink="tw5-my-wiki-0123456789abcdef"/>Load from Hive</$button>` loads the wiki from Hive.

!! Testing the plugin locally

The `hive` edition of the TiddlyWiki5 repository is a minimal wiki that contains the plugin. Start it with:

```
node ./tiddlywiki.js ./editions/hive --listen port=8080
```

Then open `http://localhost:8080` in a browser that has the Hive Keychain extension installed. The extension has to be allowed to run on the page, which Chrome asks for the first time the extension is used on a site. A single file wiki can also be built with `node ./tiddlywiki.js ./editions/hive --build index`, but then the browser needs to be given permission to run extensions on file urls.

!! Settings

|!Setting |!Default |!Description |
|Account | |The Hive account that publishes the wiki |
|Endpoint |`https://api.hive.blog` |The JSON-RPC endpoint of the Hive blockchain |
|Category |`tiddlywiki5` |The category of the root post |
|Nesting |`path` |Whether the replies are nested by the path of the tiddler titles, or all directly underneath the root post |
|Published tiddlers |`[is[tiddler]] -[prefix[$:/]] +[sort[title]]` |The filter that selects the tiddlers that are published |
|Front end |`https://hive.blog` |The base url of the Hive front end, used to build the links |
|Pull mode |`overwrite` |Whether loading overwrites the existing tiddlers, or only adds the ones that are missing |
